  "interface": {
    "model": "Explicit plain_model / model_factory adapters implement the one ModelFactory<M,S> contract. Llm binds the original borrowed schema and returns a higher-ranked borrowed async callable; &L and Rc<L> forward without cloning L. Output:Into<Raw> is required only by plain adapter revalidation, not the structured factory path.",
    "loader": "MessageLoader::load receives the original &Rc<Request<P,I>>. It can retain full call/payload identity after command+handler release while returning borrowed or shared messages. NoMessages creates a fresh shared empty collection per invocation.",
    "handler": "brain_handler borrows LlmCall and BrainPorts. Polling handle performs factory, awaited loader, schema lookup/bind, awaited invocation and the existing llm.decode. Declared failures retain their original typed CallValue causes. Native futures are lazy and local.",
    "causeFamily": "The actual builtin AGENT_TURN_SCHEMA plus a caller-owned ~15line delegating Schema/cause enum preserves distinct Model(Rc<OpaqueFailure<borrowedContext>>) and Schema(Rc<StructuredOutputError>) identities at factory/loader/bind/invoke/parse. No global error mapper or LlmCall change.",
    "bounds": "No blanket Clone/Serialize/Send/static on opaque payload, messages, model, output, error, schema or host context. The real Runtime application provides its own Cause serialization projection only at the existing command-wire boundary; pure opaque family test requires no serde.",
    "sharedChanges": "Only additive agent/mod.rs export. No LlmCall/core/runtime/command scheduling or parser/schema framework edits.",
    "lint": "One method-level #[expect(clippy::type_complexity, reason=...)] is justified by the actual borrowed higher-ranked async binding; loader async_fn_in_trait allowance documents intentional local non-Send futures."
  },
